      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case in which a sudden communication between the pressure and balloon inflation lumens of a percutaneous transluminal angioplasty (PTCA) catheter angiographically mimicked dissection of the coronary artery. This case illustrates a previously undescribed catheter artifact that must be differentiated from other complications of PTCA."},
